{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The first fruits of your labors.</b> Meaning, to exclude what enters the possession of a non-Jew, which is not 'your labors' — and similarly, He excluded this by saying ״קְצִירְכֶם״ (Leviticus 23:10), as they expounded in Rosh HaShanah (Rosh HaShanah 13a), that anything whose third [stage of growth] occurred in the possession of a non-Jew, one may not bring first fruits from it."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:50.718711978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}